Example: the acquisition cost is the contribution; the price sets the value.
One FUND unit costs 100 USD, as recorded by {100 USD} on the asset posting.
Its quoted closing price on the same date is 120 USD. Only FUND is selected,
so the cash payment is outside the report and does not cancel its contribution.
Opening value is 0, net contributions are 100, and ending value is 120 USD.
Profit/loss is 120 - 0 - 100 = 20 USD; time-weighted return is 120 / 100 - 1 = 20%.
The money-weighted returns cannot be calculated because purchase and valuation
share a date; the text formatter shows their null API values as n/a.

========== API ==========

investmentPerformance({ accounts: ['Assets:Fund'], commodities: ['FUND'], from: '2024-01-01', to: '2024-01-01' })

========== API FORMAT ==========

text

========== FILE ==========

commodity USD
  default
  format 1,000.00 USD
commodity FUND
  format 1,000 FUND
account Assets:Fund
account Assets:Cash
P 2024-01-01 FUND 120 USD

2024-01-01 Purchase
  Assets:Fund  1 FUND {100 USD}
  Assets:Cash  -100 USD

========== OUTPUT ==========

Investment performance from 2024-01-01 to 2024-01-01
Instruments: 1
Opening value: 0.00 USD
Net contributions: 100.00 USD
Ending value: 120.00 USD
Profit/loss: 20.00 USD
Time-weighted return: 20.00 %
Money-weighted return (total): n/a
Money-weighted return (annualized): n/a

========== WARNINGS ==========
